window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_main-9c4422457e416442"]={"key":"ny_main-9c4422457e416442","group":"ny_main","uid":"9c4422457e416442","rank":82,"title":"foxhollow authorized premium dispute response","occupation":"customer_service_representatives","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_main","prompt":"You are the customer service representative Mikkel Wickramasinghe at Foxhollow Industries, reviewing a draft response to Ravensmoor Freight after Camila Magnusson disputed an automatic insurance-premium withdrawal. Astrid Hutchins needs the corrected case response this week to decide how the payment authorization should be handled, and Mikkel Radulescu will review the classification boundary for compliance. The mixed case record shows that Camila was enrolled in recurring electronic payment for the same policy in both periods: a $1,240 withdrawal on 14 February 2024 and a $1,410 withdrawal on 14 February 2025. A renewal notice dated 31 January 2025 showed the current premium and policy reference. The record contains no cancellation or withdrawal of authorization before the current debit, no report that credentials were stolen or impersonated, and no other account-takeover indicator; Camila says she expected an invoice and did not understand that the renewal would be collected automatically. The draft calls the transaction “fraud,” says the authorization is invalid, and promises reimbursement, although those statements do not line up cleanly with the record. Foxhollow is transitioning from its legacy dispute classifications to a new taxonomy, while staff have been using “fraud” as shorthand for almost any customer-disputed transaction. The case also touches compliance and payment operations: your response must show where a customer-service record ends and where a formal fraud determination or payment-authority action belongs, without making that determination or taking that action yourself. Write one corrected, audience-specific, reusable case-response document for Astrid. It must state a bounded decision, compare the two premium periods and explain the material change, identify and correct the defects in the draft, distinguish the evidence-supported case classification from any legal or fraud conclusion, and give Astrid concrete record-keeping and ownership steps for the transition period and the final taxonomy. Include a clearly marked customer-facing passage that does not overstate what is known. Use 14 February 2025 as the evidence cut-off, do not invent private taxonomy codes or later facts, keep the wording factual rather than recommendatory, and end with the decision rather than a list of future actions. Keep it to two pages and no more than 700 words. Write the file into the top level of the working directory using exactly the filename `ravensmoor_premium_dispute_response.docx`.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `ravensmoor_premium_dispute_response.docx` — A corrected, audience-specific and reusable case-response document for Astrid Hutchins concerning Ravensmoor Freight's disputed automatic insurance-premium withdrawal. (Write the file at the top level of the solver's starting working directory.; Use exactly the specified filename.; Keep the document to no more than two pages and 700 words.; Use factual, bounded language and do not invent private taxonomy codes, later facts, legal conclusions, or a reimbursement outcome.; Include both an internal case-response component and a clearly marked customer-facing passage.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/ravensmoor_premium_dispute_response.docx","bytes":40283,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/6f07e8d685db24dfdef53e5ad2bb8ecf38cd8fb4fd89fb0a47c9fc76f7a2974c.docx","sha256":"6f07e8d685db24dfdef53e5ad2bb8ecf38cd8fb4fd89fb0a47c9fc76f7a2974c","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"CORRECTED CASE RESPONSE\nPremium withdrawal dispute | Completed reusable internal form\nTo / decision owner\nAstrid Hutchins\nPrepared by\nMikkel Wickramasinghe | Customer Service\nCase\nFoxhollow Industries | Ravensmoor Freight | Camila Magnusson\nEvidence cut-off\nInformation reviewed through 14 February 2025 only\n1. Record facts and premium comparison\nAuthorization history\nRecurring electronic payment was recorded for the same policy across both comparison periods.\nPrior period\n$1,240 withdrawn on 14 February 2024\nCurrent period\n$1,410 withdrawn on 14 February 2025. The 31 January 2025 renewal notice showed this premium and the policy reference; the debit aligns with that notice.\nMaterial change\n$170 increase ($1,410 - $1,240), approximately 13.7%\nReview limits\nNo cancellation or withdrawal of authorization was recorded before the current debit. The reviewed record contains no report of stolen credentials, impersonation, or another account-takeover indicator; their absence from the record is not a finding that they were impossible.\nCustomer account\nCamila Magnusson said she expected an invoice and did not understand that the renewal would be collected automatically.\n2. Draft defects corrected\nDraft defect\nEvidence-limited correction\n'Fraud' case label\nReplace with customer dispute - renewal collection/invoice expectation. A disagreement about expected invoicing is not, by itself, evidence of an unauthorized transaction; fraud is not established on the reviewed record.\n'Authorization is invalid'\nRemove. Recurring-payment history, the matched renewal notice/policy reference, and no recorded cancellation support authorization on file at the debit. This is not a legal-validity finding.\nReimbursement promise\nRemove. No reimbursement outcome or approval is recorded, and this customer-service response does not promise one.\n\n\n3. Classification, roles, and transition record\nCustomer-service classification\nCustomer dispute - renewal collection/invoice expectation. The reviewed evidence does not substantiate an unauthorized transaction.\nFormal fraud boundary\nNo formal fraud determination is made by Customer Service. Such a determination requires appropriate compliance or investigative authority and evidence beyond this classification; review boundary: Mikkel Radulescu.\nPayment-authorization boundary\nThe record supports authorization on file at the debit date. Changing, suspending, or closing authorization belongs to Payment Operations / Vera Chidozie.\nLegacy classification\nRetain during the transition from the legacy dispute classification to the new taxonomy: customer dispute - recurring renewal collection/invoice expectation (no fraud conclusion).\nFinal taxonomy classification\nProvisional plain-language mapping, pending Mikkel Radulescu's confirmation: customer disagreement about recurring renewal collection/invoice expectation. Same case meaning; no private code is recorded.\nTransition record / owner\nKeep both labels, their same-meaning cross-reference, and the evidence basis in the case record. On confirmation, record the final taxonomy description and retain legacy history. Astrid Hutchins retains this corrected response; payment authority remains with Payment Operations.\n4. Customer-facing passage\nCUSTOMER-FACING PASSAGE\nThank you for explaining that you expected an invoice and did not realize the renewal premium would be collected automatically. Our review through 14 February 2025 shows recurring electronic payment for this policy, including a $1,240 withdrawal on 14 February 2024 and the disputed $1,410 withdrawal on 14 February 2025. The $170 (about 13.7%) increase matches the premium and policy reference in the 31 January 2025 renewal notice. The record reviewed does not establish that the withdrawal was unauthorized. Payment-authorization handling is separate; this response does not promise reimbursement.\n5. Decision\nFINAL BOUNDED DECISION\nBased solely on the record available through 14 February 2025, classify this as a customer dispute about renewal collection and invoice expectation, not as an established fraud matter. The reviewed evidence does not substantiate that the 14 February 2025 withdrawal was unauthorized and supports an authorization-on-file finding at the debit date; it does not determine fraud, legal authorization, payment disposition, or any change to the authorization.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submission contains exactly the required DOCX deliverable with the specified filename.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Top-level directory listing and document metadata.","grader_hint":"Verify that ravensmoor_premium_dispute_response.docx exists, is a valid DOCX, and no alternate deliverable is being used."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX opens and renders as a readable document without corruption or missing body content.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Successful DOCX parsing and rendered pages.","grader_hint":"Open or convert the file offline; deduct if the document is unreadable, blank, materially clipped, or structurally corrupt."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The rendered document is no more than two pages.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Rendered page count.","grader_hint":"Count rendered pages using an office renderer or PDF conversion."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document contains no more than 700 words while remaining a complete case response.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Extracted document text and word count.","grader_hint":"Count substantive document words, excluding only obvious page metadata or automated field codes."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies Astrid Hutchins as the intended internal reader or decision owner.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Named addressee, audience statement, or equivalent internal heading.","grader_hint":"Look for Astrid Hutchins in an audience-appropriate context, not merely in an unrelated name list."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies Foxhollow Industries, Ravensmoor Freight, and Camila Magnusson in the case context.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Case identification and narrative text.","grader_hint":"Confirm that the entities and customer are correctly associated with the disputed premium withdrawal."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document states that its evidence and assessment are bounded as of 14 February 2025.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"As-of date or evidence-cutoff statement.","grader_hint":"Accept an equivalent formulation such as 'information available through 14 February 2025'; do not accept an undated general statement."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document acknowledges the transition from the legacy dispute classification to the new taxonomy.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Transition statement or classification fields.","grader_hint":"The transition must be connected to this case rather than mentioned as a generic corporate fact."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document distinguishes the case record's evidence from conclusions that would require unavailable or separate authority.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Evidence section, qualification, or boundary statement.","grader_hint":"Credit when the document makes clear what the records establish and what they do not establish."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document records the prior-period premium withdrawal as $1,240 on 14 February 2024.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Prior-period comparison field or narrative.","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent currency formatting if the amount and date are unambiguous."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document records the current-period premium withdrawal as $1,410 on 14 February 2025.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Current-period comparison field or narrative.","grader_hint":"The current amount must be tied to the disputed withdrawal, not merely mentioned elsewhere."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document states or calculates the absolute increase between the two premiums as $170 ±$1.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Comparison calculation.","grader_hint":"Check that the direction and arithmetic are correct: current premium less prior premium."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document states or calculates the premium increase as approximately 13.7% ±0.1 percentage points.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Percentage comparison.","grader_hint":"Use $170 divided by $1,240; accept sensible rounding within the stated tolerance."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies the 31 January 2025 renewal notice as evidence for the current premium and policy reference.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Evidence list or comparison narrative.","grader_hint":"The notice must be linked to the current-period amount or policy, not listed without relevance."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document states that recurring electronic payment was in place for the policy across the relevant periods.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Authorization history statement.","grader_hint":"Credit only if recurring authorization is tied to this policy and not described as a one-time payment."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document connects the current debit to the renewal notice's policy reference and premium amount.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Evidence-to-conclusion linkage.","grader_hint":"The response should show that the current debit aligns with the renewal record rather than merely repeating both amounts."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document records that no cancellation or withdrawal of payment authorization was recorded before the current debit.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Authorization-history finding.","grader_hint":"Look for a bounded statement about the records reviewed, not an absolute claim that cancellation was impossible."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document records that the case record contains no report of stolen credentials, impersonation, or another account-takeover indicator.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Evidence limitation or fraud-boundary statement.","grader_hint":"Accept a concise equivalent, provided it is framed as absence from the reviewed record."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document accurately describes Camila Magnusson's account of expecting an invoice and not understanding that the renewal would be collected automatically.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Customer statement summary.","grader_hint":"The response must preserve the customer's actual concern without converting it into a claim of credential theft."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document makes the professionally defensible distinction between a customer disagreement about an expected invoice or renewal collection and evidence of an unauthorized transaction.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Case classification rationale.","grader_hint":"A strong response uses the available authorization and account evidence to avoid treating customer dissatisfaction alone as proof of unauthorized use."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document explains where the commonly used 'customer dispute equals fraud' shorthand stops applying in this case.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Terminology or classification rationale.","grader_hint":"Credit when the response identifies the evidentiary boundary rather than simply banning the word fraud without explanation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document does not present fraud as an established fact on the available record.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Use of qualified terminology throughout the document.","grader_hint":"Look for careful language such as 'not established on the reviewed record'; do not credit a document that repeats the draft's accusation as fact."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document states that any formal fraud determination requires the appropriate compliance or investigative authority and evidence beyond the customer-service classification.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Functional-boundary statement.","grader_hint":"The response should identify the need for proper authority without pretending to perform that determination."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document gives one clear, bounded case decision rather than presenting competing classifications or leaving the core classification unresolved.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Decision statement and surrounding rationale.","grader_hint":"The decision should be a customer-service classification grounded in the record, not a legal verdict."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document explicitly states that the reviewed evidence does not establish that the withdrawal was unauthorized.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Bounded conclusion.","grader_hint":"Accept careful equivalents such as 'unauthorized use is not substantiated by the available record'; reject an unqualified finding of authorization if it overstates the evidence."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document treats the payment authorization as supported by the record at the time of the debit while reserving any final operational action to the responsible payment function.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Authorization-status conclusion and authority reservation.","grader_hint":"Credit the nuanced distinction between evidence of an authorization on file and authority to change or close it."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document keeps transaction classification, fraud determination, and payment-authorization status as separate propositions.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Structure and wording of the decision section.","grader_hint":"Each proposition should have its own scope or qualification; a single loaded label for all three fails."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies and corrects the draft's use of 'fraud' as the case label.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Defect-correction field or comparison statement.","grader_hint":"The correction must be explicit enough for Astrid to see what was wrong with the draft."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies and corrects the draft's unsupported statement that the authorization is invalid.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Defect-correction field or authorization analysis.","grader_hint":"Credit only if the response explains why the draft's categorical statement exceeds the reviewed evidence."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies and corrects the draft's promise of reimbursement.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Defect-correction field or customer-facing wording.","grader_hint":"The replacement must avoid promising a refund or asserting that reimbursement has been approved."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document links each material conclusion to at least one specific record fact rather than relying on a conclusory label.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rationale and evidence references.","grader_hint":"Check the classification, authorization, and draft-correction conclusions separately for factual support."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document provides a plain-language legacy classification for this case that is consistent with the bounded decision.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Legacy classification field or narrative.","grader_hint":"Do not require a private numeric code; assess whether the legacy description reflects a customer dispute without asserting fraud."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document provides a plain-language final-taxonomy classification for this case that is consistent with the same underlying decision.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Final taxonomy field or narrative.","grader_hint":"Assess semantic classification, not an invented exact code."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The legacy and final-taxonomy descriptions refer to the same case meaning and do not imply contradictory outcomes.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Side-by-side mapping or cross-reference.","grader_hint":"A mapping that calls the case fraud in one scheme and ordinary customer disagreement in the other is inconsistent unless the distinction is explicitly and defensibly explained."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document marks the taxonomy mapping as transitional or subject to final confirmation rather than presenting a locally invented mapping as authoritative.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Transition qualification.","grader_hint":"Credit when provisional status is visible and connected to the lack of a supplied private code list."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document avoids fabricating private legacy codes, new taxonomy codes, policy numbers, or evidence not provided in the case record.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All document text and labels.","grader_hint":"Names, dates, amounts, and facts in the request may be used; invented internal identifiers or unsupported events should not appear."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document gives concrete transition-period record-keeping and ownership steps that are within the recipient's operational context.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Transition-period actions or ownership fields.","grader_hint":"Steps should be specific enough to execute, such as retaining both classifications, recording the evidence basis, and assigning confirmation to the responsible owner, without prescribing a customer outcome."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document gives concrete steps for carrying the case into the final taxonomy once the taxonomy is confirmed.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Final-taxonomy handling instructions.","grader_hint":"Look for a clear treatment of later confirmation, mapping, or record update rather than a vague 'follow up later.'"},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The transition and final-taxonomy steps identify an accountable owner or function without assigning the customer-service representative authority they do not have.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Ownership statements.","grader_hint":"Credit when compliance/taxonomy ownership and payment-authority ownership are distinguishable from case documentation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies any remaining evidence limitation or unresolved question as a limitation, rather than filling the gap with an unsupported assertion.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Limitations or open-evidence statement.","grader_hint":"A good response can note that the record does not establish fraud or a later authorization change without treating that absence as proof of impossibility."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The clearly marked customer-facing passage explains the premium change and dispute status in plain, respectful language.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Customer-facing passage.","grader_hint":"Assess readability and whether the passage accurately reflects the $1,240-to-$1,410 change and the customer's stated concern."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The customer-facing passage does not accuse Camila or Ravensmoor Freight of fraud, promise reimbursement, or claim a final legal outcome.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Customer-facing language.","grader_hint":"Credit careful, non-accusatory wording that states what the record supports and what remains with the responsible function."},{"rubric_item_id":"R43","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document marks compliance or investigative review as the boundary for a formal fraud determination.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Role-boundary language.","grader_hint":"The response should refer the determination boundary to the appropriate function without making a referral sound like a finding of fraud."},{"rubric_item_id":"R44","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document marks payment operations or the authorization owner as the boundary for changing, suspending, or closing the payment authorization.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Payment-operations boundary language.","grader_hint":"Do not credit a document that directs the CSR to invalidate or retain the authorization as an operational action."},{"rubric_item_id":"R45","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document does not treat facts or guidance after 14 February 2025 as part of the evidentiary basis.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Dates and temporal qualifications throughout the document.","grader_hint":"Check for unsupported later events, current-status claims, or uncited changes to the case."},{"rubric_item_id":"R46","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The same careful distinction between customer disagreement, unauthorized transaction, fraud determination, and authorization status is maintained in the internal and customer-facing portions.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-section terminology audit.","grader_hint":"A customer-safe simplification may be shorter, but it must not reverse or overstate the internal decision."},{"rubric_item_id":"R47","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document is reusable as a case-response form or template while remaining completed for this specific case.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Field labels, clearly separated case values, and reusable wording.","grader_hint":"Credit a structure that another representative could adapt without mistaking generic prompts for facts, while still containing the present case response."},{"rubric_item_id":"R48","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document is practically navigable and editable for an internal reviewer under time pressure.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered document and editable structure.","grader_hint":"Assess scanability, meaningful labels, hierarchy, and whether the decision, evidence, defects, boundary, and transition handling can be found quickly."},{"rubric_item_id":"R49","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document presents facts and bounded determinations without recommending a customer outcome or taking an operational action on behalf of Astrid, compliance, or payment operations.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Tone and action language throughout.","grader_hint":"Administrative ownership and record-preservation steps are acceptable; recommendations to refund, deny, suspend, or close the authorization are not."},{"rubric_item_id":"R50","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document ends with one clear bounded decision, not with a future-actions list or an unresolved alternative.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Final substantive paragraph or decision field.","grader_hint":"The closing should state the case decision and its evidentiary limits; transition steps may appear earlier but must not replace the conclusion."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"This is a high-stakes customer-service and compliance communication for an insurance-payment dispute during a classification-taxonomy transition. The practitioner must turn a lightly defective draft into a usable record without exceeding customer-service authority.","difficulty_sources":["Material ambiguity between a customer disagreement about collection expectations and an unauthorized-transaction allegation.","A common but unsafe fraud shorthand must be bounded in a setting where it does not fit the available evidence.","The response must preserve one meaning across a legacy classification and an emerging taxonomy without a supplied private code list.","Customer service overlaps with compliance investigation and payment-authorization operations, requiring a clear authority boundary without overstepping.","The practitioner must lightly correct an existing response while comparing two premium periods and preserving an as-of evidence boundary."],"authoring_plan":{"reference_files":[],"source_model":{"inputs":"No reference files. The build agent should treat the facts embedded in the request as the complete frozen case record.","as_of_date":"2025-02-14","case_entities":{"company":"Foxhollow Industries","customer_organization":"Ravensmoor Freight","customer":"Camila Magnusson","customer_service_representative":"Mikkel Wickramasinghe","decision_owner":"Astrid Hutchins","compliance_or_investigative_boundary":"Mikkel Radulescu","payment_authority_boundary":"Vera Chidozie"},"facts":["Recurring electronic payment was in place for the same insurance policy across both comparison periods.","The prior-period withdrawal was $1,240 on 2024-02-14.","The current-period withdrawal was $1,410 on 2025-02-14.","The renewal notice dated 2025-01-31 showed the current premium and policy reference.","The reviewed record contains no cancellation or withdrawal of authorization before the current debit.","The reviewed record contains no report of stolen credentials, impersonation, or another account-takeover indicator.","Camila expected an invoice and did not understand that the renewal would be collected automatically.","The draft called the transaction fraud, called the authorization invalid, and promised reimbursement.","The organization is transitioning from legacy dispute classifications to a new taxonomy.","No proprietary code list is supplied; the solver must use plain-language descriptions and must not fabricate private codes."]},"gold_content_requirements":{"decision_logic":["Calculate the premium increase as $170 and approximately 13.7%.","Treat the renewal notice, recurring authorization, matching policy reference, and absence of a recorded cancellation as evidence relevant to authorization at the time of debit.","Treat Camila's expectation of an invoice and lack of understanding about automatic collection as a customer communication or expectation dispute, not standalone proof of unauthorized use.","Do not convert the absence of takeover indicators into a categorical claim that fraud was impossible.","Separate the customer-service classification from a formal fraud determination and from the operational act of changing payment authorization.","Use one semantically consistent plain-language classification across the legacy and final taxonomy, with a visible transition qualification.","State a bounded case decision that the available record does not substantiate an unauthorized transaction and supports an authorization-on-file finding at the debit date, while reserving formal authority to the relevant functions.","Replace the draft's fraud assertion, invalid-authorization assertion, and reimbursement promise with evidence-limited language."],"transition_handling":["Retain the legacy classification for continuity during transition.","Record the corresponding plain-language final-taxonomy category or pending mapping without inventing a private code.","Identify who confirms the final taxonomy mapping and who owns any payment-authorization action.","Keep record-keeping and ownership steps administrative and factual rather than recommending a refund, denial, suspension, or closure."],"customer_language":["Explain the change from $1,240 to $1,410 and connect it to the renewal notice.","Acknowledge the customer's expectation of an invoice and confusion about automatic collection.","Avoid accusing the customer or organization of fraud.","Avoid promising reimbursement or stating a final legal conclusion.","Clearly mark the passage as customer-facing and keep it consistent with the internal decision."],"document_constraints":["The final DOCX must be usable as a completed reusable case-response form or template.","The final substantive text must close on the bounded decision, not on transition actions.","The document must fit within the request's two-page and 700-word limits."]},"gold_review_method":"Construct an offline reference response using only the embedded facts and ordinary insurance customer-service, payments, and compliance practice. Walk every rubric predicate against the rendered DOCX and verify that all factual claims are limited to the frozen record, the two classification descriptions agree, the functional boundaries are explicit, and the document remains usable within the cap."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"mixed_media_bundle","structure":"supplied_template"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"corrected_case_response","filename":"ravensmoor_premium_dispute_response.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A corrected, audience-specific and reusable case-response document for Astrid Hutchins concerning Ravensmoor Freight's disputed automatic insurance-premium withdrawal.","required":true,"constraints":["Write the file at the top level of the solver's starting working directory.","Use exactly the specified filename.","Keep the document to no more than two pages and 700 words.","Use factual, bounded language and do not invent private taxonomy codes, later facts, legal conclusions, or a reimbursement outcome.","Include both an internal case-response component and a clearly marked customer-facing passage."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"communicate_stakeholders","work_product":"form_or_template","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world_with_assumptions"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"customer_service_representatives","sector":"finance_insurance","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":2.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"domain_expert","reviewer_policy":"Have an experienced insurance customer-service or payments-compliance reviewer assess the completed DOCX against the rubric, with particular attention to the distinction between customer disagreement, unauthorized transaction, fraud determination, and authorization status. A second independent reviewer may resolve close judgments about wording, usability, and functional boundaries.","minimum_reviewers":1,"known_limitations":["No proprietary Foxhollow code list is supplied, so grading must evaluate semantic consistency of plain-language legacy and final-taxonomy classifications rather than exact private codes.","The case facts are embedded in the request rather than provided as separate source files; the grader should not expect citations to nonexistent attachments."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:12:41+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:12:41+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:12:41+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:12:41+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_main/runs/9c4422457e416442","declared_deliverables":["ravensmoor_premium_dispute_response.docx"]};
